  body: "# Individual treatment and free in-patient conditions\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    hospital guidance requires its free in-patient conditions together and treats medical or nursing treatment
    as an individual factual question, rather than assuming every resident of an establishment receives
    it.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source distinguishes professional medical or nursing treatment
    from straightforward unqualified care and includes private-patient exceptions. Funding, prescribed
    legal basis, in-patient status and the benefit-specific scope remain necessary; no conclusion about
    an individual’s care setting or entitlement follows.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 18020,
    PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80d88aed915d74e33fcbde/dmgch18.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 18: Hospital in-patients.\n- [DMG 18021, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80d88aed915d74e33fcbde/dmgch18.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 18: Hospital in-patients.\n- [DMG 18024, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80d88aed915d74e33fcbde/dmgch18.pdf#page=8)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 18: Hospital in-patients.\n- [DMG 18025, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80d88aed915d74e33fcbde/dmgch18.pdf#page=8)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 18: Hospital in-patients.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch18`: PDF SHA-256 `cb377d4db23653485a8a4c10e1ea19da1bba9bb9aad731e382e22b53fc4fa863`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `7953f5a17805c8271ec4bcc926e0414ba0b19c358597faaf4eee431006a456a8`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The treatment passage expressly requires a factual finding for each person and warns
      against assuming all residents have the same treatment status.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch18/0008
      quote: "18025   Whether a person is receiving treatment is a question of fact. It cannot be assumed\n\
        \        that because one person is receiving treatment in a hospital or similar\n        establishment,
        that another person in the same establishment can automatically be\n        regarded as receiving
        treatment. But the fact that a person is an in-patient in a\n                                \
        \                                                                          1\n        hospital
        is strong evidence that the person is receiving medical or other treatment .\n               \
        \                                                                                   1 R(S) 26/54"
      locator: DMG 18025
